.git
.gitignore
.pytest_cache

# Environment files must never enter the image.
#
# Two separate problems this prevents:
#  1. Secret leakage. `COPY . .` was baking the root .env — which holds a live
#     OPENROUTER_API_KEY — into an image layer, where anyone who can pull the
#     image can read it. Runtime config belongs in the platform's secret store.
#  2. A broken production build. `COPY frontend/ ./` fed frontend/.env to
#     `npm run build`, baking VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8011 into the
#     bundle. The container serves the SPA and the API on one origin, so the
#     browser would have called the *user's own machine* and every request would
#     have failed. With no .env present, VITE_API_BASE_URL is empty and the
#     client correctly issues same-origin relative requests.
.env
*.env
**/.env
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
logs/
error.log
error_full.txt
train_log.txt
training_output.txt
training_output2.txt
visualize_output.txt
test.txt
